            <h2>Route Overview: Alexandria to Norfolk</h2>
            <p>Traveling from <b>Alexandria to Norfolk</b>by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect Northern Virginia with the Hampton Roads region. This route offers passengers a relaxed alternative to driving or flying, especially popular with leisure travelers, students, military personnel, and weekend travelers. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the service offers comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and plenty of picturesque views through Virginia's diverse landscapes. </p>
            <p>The route is primarily served by Amtrak's Northeast Regional, offering multiple daily departures between Alexandria Union Station and Norfolk's Harbor Park Station. Compared to road travel on the often-congested I-95 and I-64 corridors, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic. It makes city-center-to-city-center travel easy, without worrying about parking or rental cars in downtown Norfolk. </p>
