            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The <b>Alexandria-to-Norfolk</b> train route runs through the heart of Virginia, traveling southeast from the Potomac River through the Piedmont region, past Richmond, and into the coastal plains of Hampton Roads. Passengers get spectacular views of Virginia's diverse landscapes, from rolling farmland to coastal wetlands, making the journey more than just transit; it's a relaxed, picturesque experience through one of America's most historically significant states. </p>
            <p>The route passes through key cities and towns such as Fredericksburg, Richmond, Petersburg, before reaching Norfolk. Along the way, travelers can enjoy natural scenery, including Civil War battlefields, tobacco country, pine forests, and the transition to coastal Virginia's maritime landscape. </p>
