            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Alexandria to Norfolk? </h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 4 hours 13 minutes to 4 hours 41 minutes, depending on the service and the number of stops. </p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Alexandria to Norfolk? </h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Northeast Regional, which can complete the journey in approximately 4 hours and 13 minutes with direct service. </p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Alexandria to Norfolk cost? </h3>
            <p>
                Ticket prices generally fall between:
                $26-$45 for early booking
                $45-$85 for standard fares
                $85-$150 for last-minute Coach travel
                $75-$150 for Business Class
                $150-$290+ for last-minute Business Class
            </p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Alexandria to Norfolk? </h3>
            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Northeast Regional trains on this segment are direct, so there's no need for transfers. </p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard? </h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, free Wi-Fi, power outlets, a café car, and luggage space. Business Class includes complimentary non-alcoholic beverages and priority boarding. </p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving? </h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving on I-95 and I-64 may take 3-4.5 hours, while the train is generally reliable and stress-free, especially during rush hour or bad weather. </p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Alexandria to Norfolk in one day? </h3>
            <p>Technically, yes, but the schedule makes it challenging with only 3 daily departures. The morning train arrives late morning, and the evening return departs around 4:00-5:00 PM, leaving limited time. Most travelers prefer an overnight stay. </p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Alexandria do trains depart from? </h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Alexandria Union Station, located in historic Old Town Alexandria. Airport connections exist via Metro from DCA and IAD. </p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Norfolk? </h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Norfolk Harbor Park Station, conveniently located in downtown Norfolk and easily accessible by HRT buses, The Tide Light Rail, and rideshare. </p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class worth it for this 4+ hour trip? </h3>
            <p>For the 4+ hour journey between Alexandria and Norfolk, Coach offers excellent value. Business Class is worthwhile for travelers needing a quiet, productive environment with complimentary beverages and extra legroom, making the extended trip more comfortable. </p>







